our next award is very special it honors  a 50-year career in our in our industry  and to do the honors we have a special  presenter so while i get back to go  there and take a little breather would  you please welcome the distinguished  actor and director dennis hopper  what a great job she's doing such a  difficult one  well you know  to give this award tonight is probably  the greatest honor i've ever had  bestowed on me when i  when i opened the letter that asked me  to give this award i just uh i thought  boy if you just live long enough you  know  in the winter of  1946  after a tour in the navy  joe lombardi moved to southern  california from his home in new jersey  he got a job of building houses out in  the valley  where he was approached and asked if he  could  build a circular staircase for a motion  picture production  and the rest is  film history  joe's first special effects work was for  the three stooges at columbia pictures  now uh while joe's always been noted for  his concerns about safety on the set  i'm pretty sure it's just a rumor that  when moe went like this  that it was joe who told larry to do  this you know  anyway  joe went on to work on set construction  and sequentially special effects on the  i love lucy show which eventually led to  long-term relationships with danny  thomas and red skelton  it was lucy who gave joe the name for  his newly founded company in 1960 when  she remarked that his talent was  unlimited thus special effects unlimited  was born  over the years joe has supervised  special effects on a list of films as  long as your arm  it's an incredible uh it's incredible  work  and it's been an incredible career  which i'm happy to report is still going  very strong  uh this uh this award of con  commendation reads to joe lombardi  in celebration of 50 years in the motion  picture industry  his knowledge and leadership in the  field of pyrotechnics and special  effects along with his uncompromising  promotion of safety on the set have  established the standard for today's  special effects technicians  it's a pleasure and a great honor to  present this award to the joe lombardi  i want to thank dennis especially dennis  and i have been involved in apocalypse  now super mario brothers  and a few specialties that he had on his  own  over there  this is a very special moment for me and  i feel fortunate to be here tonight  looking back at my career it looks like  years have gone by too quickly  i think it's because i love this  business  and it provided with me and my family  and i thank god that i have a great  career and helped  make a lot of shows traveled all over  the world and met a lot of people  there are some special people who  deserve my thanks  lucille ball who gave me a break in the  business and who encouraged me to pursue  special effects  desi arnaz one of the smartest producers  ever  danny thomas a hell of an actor a  humanitarian  and a generous friend and the greatest  comedian red skelton  directors john irving francis coppola  and john milius for believing in me and  let me do things i like to make their  films exciting i also want to thank  my close friend don rogers as well as  kevin pike ray feeney pete clark and my  partner gabe develop  who have had a role in this award last  but not least i want to thank my  daughter susan who is here tonight along  with my son paul whose accomplishment  and special effects have made me very  very proud i wish her mother were alive  to share this with me  in closing i want to thank the academy  and the scientific award for this  special award you have really made my  day thank you  you
 

